# mutgap_tex_legacy_heap_discard: In-process a heap is a legacy heap (private, paged through a transfer buffer). A fill of a buffer placed in it stays on the host. 63 discards the heap, which makes it volatile without synchronizing; the next exec that lists it prepares it again (needsPrepare), devolatilizes it, finds it host-valid and returns without copying the guest pages over it: a copy out of the heap buffer still shows the fill, and the guest pages still hold their pattern. (Were the OS to purge the volatile heap in between, the prepare would page the guest bytes in: under no memory pressure it does not.)
